    energy_reserve_coopt: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-82 miso-219 (2026-09-05, ZERO-SOLVE, no verdict change, keeper unchanged) MEASURES THE CO-OPT'S REACH IN THE C3a-2025 OBJECT AND REFUSES THE WHOLE REQUIREMENT-REPAIR FAMILY ARITHMETICALLY: miso_rbdc - the family carrying the $3,500 MISO_RESERVE_DEMAND_CURVE_MAX - records ZERO shortfall in ALL 26,280 hours of 2023-2025, and in the top-15 measured-price Jun-Jul hours the family duals are exactly 0.000 in 2023 and 2024 and fire in only 2 of 15 hours in 2025, capped at the $98 Reg+Spin step. The blocker is NOT the curve, the penalty or the requirement: for the RBDC to bind at all the requirement would have to be 10.62x (2023) / 6.40x (2024) / 3.26x (2025) the published one, measured against the fleet's OWN REALIZED annual-max thermal output (23,525 / 14,016 / 5,679 MW of headroom over a 2,445 / 2,595 / 2,515 MW requirement) - nameplate headroom makes every multiple larger, so this is the conservative reading. Restoring the 2025 Midwest requirement collapse in full is +463 MW and reverting to the static published MSSC + 400 MW basis is +0.9 GW (1.35x); both are an order of magnitude short of 3.26x. results/calibration/FINDING-miso219-evening-scarcity-tail-2026-09-05.md; probe scripts/probes/_miso219_evening_tail_phase0.py; record _miso219_evening_tail.json" },
