    offer_curve_by_group: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-223 (results/calibration/FINDING-miso223-committed-band-debody-2026-09-06.md) — CELL STAYS K, one PARAMETERISATION refuted, not the mechanism: the committed-band de-lift (revert miso-220's x1.10 on `committed` only, 11 already-registered miso-217 values, zero new numbers) DIED on its own pre-registered screen gate G-1, moving the 2024 body -$0.653 against a declared -$1.0..-$2.2. Direction right, magnitude ~35% of predicted. THE TRANSFERABLE RESULT: `committed` carries 47.4% of lifted-class ENERGY but sets the price far less often, so a body-aimed arm belongs in econlo / the econc00-05 coal ladder / mustrun, and its footprint must be measured as MARGINAL FREQUENCY, not annual energy — the wrong-proxy error was in the PREREG's own metric. G-2 confinement PASSED (tail -$0.989), so the mechanism is real and well-behaved, merely small. Screen only: 2024 alone, bundle never registered and deleted before merge (rule 29 clause 2 + (c)); CC_REGULAR-2024 exposure UNTESTED (G-3 unscored, no metrics.json on a single-year replay). Keeper UNCHANGED. | miso-215 (2026-09-05, ZERO-SOLVE, cell UNCHANGED at K — evidence about the container, no verdict, no field, no row): the three DUTY-ROLE COHORT SPLIT curves this row registers literally under rule 28(c) — CT_INTERMEDIATE, CC_INTERMEDIATE, ST_GAS_INTERMEDIATE — carry NO phys_* keys, because pipeline/backcast_config._neutralize_generic_gas_bands names exactly five gas classes (CC_REGULAR, CC_CHP, CT_CHP, CT_PEAKER, ST_GAS) and _MISO_OFFER_CURVE deep-merges phys_* onto those same five. So offer_curves.gas_offer_margin_markup_mult returns its documented rule-24 neutral 0.0 for every band of all three, apply_gas_offer_margin skips them, and 38,501.0 MW = 58.4 % of MISO’s assembled gas capacity stays in the fully fuel-scaled multiplier form the armed gas_offer_net_revenue_margin exists to replace. Registered bands vs the parent phys_* an arm would borrow: CT_INTERMEDIATE 1.00/1.00/1.20/3.00 vs 1.025/0.687/0.691/1.00; CC_INTERMEDIATE 1.005/0.95/1.08/2.25 vs 1.005/0.887/1.008/2.25 (peak clips to 0); ST_GAS_INTERMEDIATE 1.00/1.00/1.15/2.20 vs 1.079/0.812/0.849/1.00. Full adjudication and the owner routing are on the gas_offer_net_revenue_margin cell above; FINDING-miso215-intermediate-phys-coverage-2026-09-05.md §2, §5. MISO-221 (2026-09-06, ZERO-SOLVE, cell UNCHANGED at K — evidence about the container, no verdict, no field, no row): the C3c PEAK-BAND RESHAPE is measured UNREACHABLE on this channel in every form rule 1 [R-STRUCT] carve-out (a) permits, and the arm died at rule-29 phase 0 with ZERO LP MINUTES — no screen year named, no solve, no bundle, no registration. GOVERNANCE FIRST: the charter named the knob as \"peak and pct_peaking\", but (a) admits the four band multipliers ONLY and excludes the structural shares (econ_low_share, pct_peaking) by name, so the capacity-reshape form was never admissible and needs an owner amendment; every candidate moved band multipliers only (asserted in code by _assert_scope). THE DIAGNOSIS WAS RIGHT AND THE LEVER STILL FAILS: CT_PEAKER|econ IS the dominant block above the clearing price (49.9/46.6/27.6 % of it). (1) peak x4.5 is nearly free and nearly inert — object-hour mean price moves -$0.04/-$0.03/+$3.04, 0/0/1 of 15 hours cross $200, costing only 0.0008-0.0051 TWh because the keeper's CT_PEAKER|peak band produces 0.0007/0.0019/0.0001 TWh all year; it is 4.6-12.6 % of the above-price block so the clearing point settles on the next tranche. (2) The MEAN-PRESERVING econ spread — the only reshape that protects the CT_PEAKER-2023 cell — cannot reach and moves 2023 BACKWARDS (-$0.62/+$0.53/+$2.78; ceiling $194.26 even at delta 0.88, an econ_low of 0.22), because the marginal tranche sits in the lower half of the block it re-slices. (3) The LEVEL lift has reach but no room: x1.5, the smallest tested, removes 7.74 TWh of CT_PEAKER-2023 against 0.015 TWh of C1 headroom (516x; floor-corrected bound 6.8 TWh, still 450x and ~2x outside the band) while putting 0 of 15 hours above $200 with a $52.50 ceiling. 2023 is unreachable at EVERY value — ceiling $56.47 even at x5.0 — and rule 1 condition (b) makes 2023 govern. THE MEASUREMENT THAT GENERALISES: at the model's own 2025 annual maximum (07-28 HE19, $187.04 vs actual $683.21) the capacity above the clearing price is 2,849 MW of which 2,557 MW (89.8 %) is the NON-TRANCHE block carrying no offer_curve_by_group entry at all, and that block is NOT a mixed bag: resolved by fuel_type it is 90.9/91.8/98.7 % OIL (2,898/2,898/2,856 MW above price at a cap-weighted $241.11/$248.65/$241.30), essentially the whole ~2.9 GW MISO oil fleet, on the legacy override/CSV path. So this channel controls 10.2 % of the supply that would have to be re-priced at the hour where it controls the most, and the block it cannot reach is ALREADY PRICED IN THE TAIL. miso-220's unreachable-block declaration (oil/biomass/ST_CHP) is promoted from a footnote to the finding. THE MODEL IS NOT MISSING TAIL-PRICED CAPACITY, IT IS MISSING THE TIGHTNESS TO REACH IT: ~2.9 GW at ~$241 plus ~2.5 GW between $200 and the actual in 2025, and at 2025's three tightest object hours only 329/1,044/1,719 MW separates the clearing price from $200. Reconstruction residual <= $0.14/$0.17/$1.35 against the keeper's committed duals, so the construction is not the story. CONSEQUENCE: C3c is NOT an offer-curve problem in MISO — with the reserve/scarcity family closed arithmetically (miso-219) and maxgen_emergency_tier_pricing contributing exactly $0, the remaining levers must REMOVE capacity from the stack or RE-PRICE THE NON-TRANCHE FLEET. FINDING-miso221-peak-band-reshape-2026-09-06.md; _miso221_peak_shape.json." },
    committed_band_measured_basis: { cell: "U", ev: "pjm-h6 (2026-09-14) shard seed on the BUILD, no verdict minted — U: UNTESTED HERE. Rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): PJM's measurement fills no other ISO's cell, and a transfer candidate enters as U and derives its own parameters from its own market's artifact. The mechanism is GENERIC IN FORM (it reads whichever ISO's data/raw/reference/<iso>_campd_marginal_hr_summary.csv exists) and the shared ScenarioConfig default is False, so this ISO is byte-identical and its keeper's cache key is unmoved. Before any lane tests it here it owes its own phase-0: this ISO's own registered committed bands against its own artifact, its own confinement/identity/magnitude gates, and its own rule-19 enumeration of what already prices its coal min-load block." },
