    f923_gas_price_plausibility_screen: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-49 (2026-09-08) landed it repo-wide, default ON, untested in any MISO solve. miso-247 (2026-09-09) TESTED AND ARMED IT: cell U -> K on keeper 2026-09-09-miso-247-p19-posture (full span 2023-2025, one bundle, rule 16), DETERMINATION CALIBRATED, C3c the single ledgered caveat, grade summary scored 8 / target 7 / ledgered 1 / fails 0 and DOF 41/2 -- every one IDENTICAL to the miso-245 predecessor, C3c hour counts included (3/7/11 vs 30/37/88). MISO measured 2024 footprint: 1003 plant-months in band, 2 low, 0 negative, 123 high to reference on 29 plants, 0 unscreened -- reproducing SPP-49 published MISO number exactly (EXPECTED, a plumbing check, not corroboration). Basis is rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] and NEVER the residual: an own-reported month outside [0.5, 2.0] x its OWN state measured EIA delivered-to-electric-power price is an average cost carrying a fixed transport charge over a near-zero burn denominator, on a different basis than the marginal fuel cost the LP prices. Band DECLARED and never swept; ZERO free parameters. PROMOTED WITH ITS SIBLING, WHICH CANNOT BE DECLINED: the same owner ruling P19 landed eia860.py::_apply_simple_cycle_hr_floor as a CONSTRUCTION with NO ScenarioConfig field, NO cache-key entry, SOLVE_EPOCHS empty and data.fleet.eia860 absent from SURFACE_MODULES. miso-247 G-DRIFT MEASURED it LIVE at MISO -- 55 rows / 624.8 MW in all three years, hr_after in exactly {9.0, 9.9, 39.6}, the clamp never lowering a rate -- which FALSIFIES rule 29(b) form 4 for any MISO arm at HEAD, since there is no gate to pin. A control solve was EARNED and spent on the screen year alone; it attributes the response A = arm minus control (ST_GAS +1.9155, COAL -1.7948, CT_PEAKER +1.6171, import -1.3788 TWh) against B = control minus predecessor (CT_PEAKER -0.2732, everything else under 0.08), and no class moved in B that D-1 had not predicted. DISCLOSED: THE RULE-29 SCREEN GATE G-1 FAILED -- ST_GAS realised +1.9554 TWh against a repaired-predictor +0.5964, ratio 3.279 against a [1/3, 3] band fixed before either predictor existed. The gate was SATISFIABLE (COAL 2.030, CC_REGULAR 1.140, CC_CHP 0.515 clear it) so NO BAR WAS MOVED and no repair was made; CT_PEAKER, which this session own predictor repair had moved out of scope, WOULD ALSO have failed at 4.717, reported under a duty declared before the numbers. G-2/G-3/G-4 PASS, zero collateral flips. The full span was spent on the OWNER explicit mid-session instruction and on rules 1/14, NOT on the screen authority. BANDS AT FULL MAGNITUDE, NOT NETTED: 14 scored bands toward, 9 away, zero flips. Toward -- CT_PEAKER fuelmix 2023 -3.056 to -0.687 and 2024 -1.83 to -0.482, ST_GAS 2024 -5.038 to -3.167, system gas volume 2023 -13.83 to -11.55 and 2024 -6.47 to -3.52, mean price 2023 2.11 to 1.69 and 2024 1.19 to 0.54. Away -- EVERY scored coal band (COAL_PRB 2024 -3.36 to -4.59, COAL_BIT 2024 -3.532 to -3.988, COAL_LIGNITE both years, system coal volume 2024 -7.55 to -9.27) plus mean price 2025 -2.4 to -2.86. THE COAL REGRESSION IS ROUTED, NOT ABSORBED: the model was short on BOTH gas and coal, so pricing gas correctly moved gas toward and displaced coal further below its own actual -- a SEPARATE unaddressed object and the successor first candidate. Nothing was tuned to close it. FINDING-miso247-the-P19-posture-at-MISO-2026-09-09.md." },
