    gas_offer_curve_tranches: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-152 (2026-08-11) KEEPS cell K -- the mechanism is NOT refuted -- and records a MEASURED FILL-ORDER caveat on it, closing the base-band inversion thread miso-151 section 8 named but did not open (charter B, Phase 0, NO solve, NO run registered). WHY THE BANDS INVERT: deliberately. _MISO_OFFER_CURVE grounds the committed band in the measured CAMPD part-load premium and the source comment records the PREVIOUS state (committed 0.92 < econ_low 0.95) as the defect it was fixing, so the inversion is not itself a bug. WHAT IT OPENS IS: the LP fills tranches in COST order while physics fills them in OUTPUT-POSITION order; there is NO same-plant fill-order constraint anywhere in the LP (lp/bounds.py sets col_lower = min_gen else pmin per independent column; the only group row in lp/rows.py is the hydro envelope), and MISO floors NOTHING on the CC committed tranche (pmin AND min_gen are 0.0 on all 44 CC_REGULAR committed rows, all 8760 h). So a CC plant produces its incremental bands while its 515.97 MW min-load block sits idle -- real plant p991: committed 515.97 MW @ $26.184 with econc00-02 at 36.85 MW each @ $25.122/$25.643/$26.164, all three CHEAPER than the block they physically sit on. CONFIRMED AT THREE LEVELS: source (G-1), effective mc through the real offer path (G-2: committed dearer than an econ sub in 1,167,048 of 2,312,640 plant-band-hours = 50.5 %, mean gap $0.833/MWh, ~3 of the 6 smoothed subs per plant), and a live solve_dispatch (G-3, 4/4 tests, tests/test_miso152_fillorder.py). AND IT IS IMMATERIAL: out-of-order energy is 0.36/0.31/0.45 % of CC energy (2023/24/25) against a pre-registered prior of 25 % band [5,60] -- REFUTED ~55x, below the band floor -- because the object is WIDE BUT THIN (each econ sub is 7 % of the min-load block and the price window is ~$1/MWh wide), touching 39-43 of 44 plants in 7,118/7,200/10,693 plant-hours. T-6 (reconstruction vs committed class_hourly) PASSES on CC: -1.83/-1.01/+9.42 %. NO LEVER PROPOSED: the sign is REPAIR-DEPENDENT and both limbs are small -- R-a PIN (min-load must-take whenever the plant runs, the ERCOT-141 floor_online_hours mechanism) gives +1.06/+0.87/+1.49 % CC supply, price DOWN, WRONG way for the -15.6 % miss; R-b GATE (no upper band unless the min-load block clears) gives -0.36/-0.31/-0.45 %, price UP and tiny. PREREG P-2 was registered with a band spanning zero and section 7 disclosed the author's prior expectation of UP before measuring; picking a limb to get a sign would be fitting the repair to the residual (rule 1 second half). NAMED SUCCESSOR, NOT OPENED: CT_PEAKER carries the SAME inversion with the largest gap in the fleet ($12.50-25.89/MWh, 15-30x CC's) and its 79 committed rows are as UNFLOORED as CC's, but its T-6 FAILS (+38.8/+37.9/+40.1 %; ST_GAS -38.0/-39.2/-59.3 %) so its reconstructed 1.20/0.54/6.47 % out-of-order share is DESCRIPTIVE ONLY and no verdict rests on it -- measuring it needs an instrument that reproduces CT commitment. Keeper 2026-08-09-miso-148-basis-aware UNCHANGED, fail set still {C3a, C3b}. FINDING-miso152-the-inversion-is-real-and-immaterial-2026-08-11.md; PREREG-miso152-tranche-fill-order-2026-08-11.md." },
    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED / KEEPER (miso-250, 2026-09-09) \u2014 ARMED on MISO's keeper recipe by the OWNER RULING of 2026-09-09 (handoff ADDENDUM \u00a7A7, verbatim: \"these should be promoted as keepers on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness\"), which SUPERSEDES miso-249's disposition of 41 minutes earlier (commit 7577449a 04:44 UTC \"keep BUILT and DEFAULT-OFF\"; the ruling is ff3afcf3 05:25 UTC and explicitly overrides \"the disposition guidance in PROMPT 1-5 and in \u00a7A2\"). THE INERTNESS IS UNCHANGED, REPORTED AT FULL MAGNITUDE, AND IS NOT A DISQUALIFIER. Cell I -> K on promotion, not on a residual. INDEPENDENT RE-MEASUREMENT of miso-249's census, on a different harness and against the CURRENT keeper (miso248_fullspan_K; miso-249 measured miso247_fullspan_K and states \"the keeper did not move at miso-248\" \u2014 it did, e4247c73 promoted it three minutes before miso-249 committed): print-derived share of gas capacity-hours 1.000 / 1.000 / 1.000 in 2023 / 2024 / 2025 (1,609 / 1,616 / 1,614 gas rows); delivered-gas array max |delta| 0.0 and NON-gas fuels 0.0 in every year; whole pre-LP state (fuel_prices, mc_base, demand, CFs, capacities, every FleetArrays field incl. availability/min_gen/ramp10) worst |delta| = 0 in all three years. HARNESS POWER DEMONSTRATED rather than assumed, same harness, 2023, one field at a time: gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing=False moves mc_base 292.467, coal_plant_monthly_pricing=False 60.855, f923_gas_price_plausibility_screen=False 2730.599 \u2014 the first IS the mechanism (with the print path off the trajectory the seam moves reaches the merit order). THE SEAM DOES FIRE, on the ISO-level _gas_series only: 2023 annual 2.8392 -> 3.0187 (max month gap +1.0003 Jan), 2024 2.4893 -> 2.5580 (+1.5513 Jan) \u2014 reproducing FINDING-xiso \u00a73's MISO rows to three decimals \u2014 and 2025 BYTE-IDENTICAL, the predicted inert-by-coverage STOP confirmed (basket 0.400; the drop-outs are LA .238 and MI .147 dominant, NOT the \"MN and MS\" the handoff names). Every _gas_series consumer is OFF on the keeper (coal_prb/bit_passthrough_sigmoid False, coal_prb_passthrough_tiered False, miso_offer_surface_measured False), and miso_zonal_gas_basis is a MEAN-ZERO spread orthogonal to a level. CONFIRMED ON REAL SOLVES, not only pre-LP (rule 29 screen, year 2024 named ex ante in the PRECOMMIT on the mechanism's largest measured footprint, never a residual): ARM vs CONTROL both at HEAD = 0 differing cells in system / class_hourly / class_band_hourly / reserve_family / storage, same simplex iteration count 388,398, same objective 4,777,088,612.6060 -> 4,777,088,612.6964; and ARM vs the committed keeper equals CONTROL vs the committed keeper CELL FOR CELL, so 100% of the deviation is HEAD drift and 0% is the arm. RULE 19 [R-ONE-MECH] NOTE, recommended not applied (the module is the shared seam, not MISO's file): the docstring's declared ordering (national annual < state-average monthly < measured hub index) OMITS the per-plant F923 print, which is a fourth and more-local measured level that supersedes the state-average monthly \u2014 the same omission miso-249 names independently. SUCCESSOR, recommended with evidence and NOT built (out of scope): EIA-923 Schedule-5 quantity-weighted plant receipts, already on disk (data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_fuel_costs.parquet) and already read every solve, cover EVERY MISO footprint state in all 12 months of EVERY year 2019-2025 \u2014 footprint coverage 1.000, Louisiana included \u2014 against N3045's 0.30-0.34 in 2019-2021 and 0.40 in 2025, and price Uri at MISO Feb-2021 = 13.9023 $/MMBtu vs the model's 4.42; blended on the SAME weights, zero new parameters, re-derived here independently and matching FINDING-miso249 \u00a77 to four decimals on all seven years. Three conditions: it must be DAILY (a monthly form reproduces RESULT-ercot254 \u00a73b exactly), MISO holds no `complete` marker so it cannot score 2021, and \u00a72 shows little for it to do in 2023-2025. docs/RESULT-miso-fuelvintage-ep-level-2026-09-09.md, docs/PRECOMMIT-miso-fuelvintage-ep-level-2026-09-09.md." },
