    vre_curtailment_oversupply_allocation: { cell: "U", ev: "U: UNTESTED and THE MOST DIRECTLY APPLICABLE non-SPP cell. MISO wind is the OTHER ISO where the reference-rate gross-up is LIVE AND UNCONDITIONAL at HEAD (vre_reference_rate_curtailment_grossup cell K, rate 0.048947), and miso-206/miso-234 measured exactly the defect this mechanism repairs — bound = 1.051466 x delivered in every hour, P1 wind ON the bound in 8,760/8,760 hours, re-curtailment 0.001/0.000/-0.003 %, so 100 % of the +4.7/+5.1/+5.1 TWh wind excess IS the un-recurtailed gross-up — and miso-206's own note named the correct FORM as 'price- or congestion-conditioned'. NOTHING TRANSFERS (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d)): SPP's verdict is SPP's, MISO's own footprint is unmeasured here, and miso-206 additionally recorded that its headroom is only 251 MW (0.8 % of the reserve margin) in its C3a object hours, so a re-allocation may well be immaterial there — MISO's desk must measure that itself. Row minted SPP-51c (2026-09-09) with its field, rule 28(c)." },
