    vre_reference_rate_curtailment_grossup: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-206 (2026-09-04, ZERO-SOLVE, nothing armed, no field, keeper unchanged; PREREG-miso206-wind-availability-object-hours-2026-09-04.md @ f55af87f pushed before any adjudicating statistic; FINDING-miso206-the-wind-excess-is-the-grossup-and-the-tail-is-half-the-object-2026-09-04.md; probe scripts/probes/_miso206_wind_availability_phase0.py, record _miso206_wind_availability_phase0.json). LIVE IN EVERY MISO KEEPER (the construction is unconditional for MISO wind), cell K by that fact alone. THE WIND-AVAILABILITY OBJECT IN THE C3a OBJECT HOURS IS REFUSED ON THE BOUND: N-1 the measured series rebuilt from the raw EIA930_BALANCE files reproduces production at max|diff| 0.0 on every archive-carried hour (the BALANCE Data Date for MISO is an EST label; the model/reference clock is fixed CST); N-2 bound = delivered/(1-0.048947) at 0.0000 MW and P1 wind ON the bound in 8,760/8,760 h every year (0 curtailed hours); N-3 miso-205 object set reproduced exactly. In the 15 object hours the excess is 262.3 / 285.0 / 250.6 MW (2023/24/25) = 0.6 / 0.7 / 0.8 % of miso-203 G-D broad reserve margin (42.7/38.4/30.5 GW) and 1.7 / 2.4 / 4.5 % of armed-class idle; even TOTAL removal of object-hour wind (5,359/5,822/5,120 MW) is 12.5/15.2/16.8 % of the margin, under the 25 % licensing line every year. P7 mechanism rule: excess is 2.6/1.5/1.0 % of the object net-load elevation — the wind DEFICIT there (h-o-d matched p54.5/p36.1/p36.5) is a MEASURED fact of the 930 series, not a model error; solar control identical to the digit. DEAD like the ambient derate. The +5.1 TWh/yr annual excess is a LEVEL object (constant 5.15 % in every hour) that no scarce-hour lever owns; its form defect is named in the base row. INDEPENDENTLY REPRODUCED at miso-234 (2026-09-07, ZERO-LP, keeper unchanged at 2026-09-07-miso-233-spp-hourly, cell verdict UNCHANGED at K), on an OWNER QUESTION asked mid-session ('why is wind overproducing, do we need MISO HSL data'). miso-206's N-2 reproduces to the digit on a different instrument (bench classFull + committed class_hourly sidecars instead of the raw BALANCE rebuild): reference rate 4.895 % (latest contributing year 2024), gross-up x1.05147; potential = actual x 1.05147 = 96.4352/103.3076/104.0300 TWh against a MODEL 96.4347/103.3076/104.0335, so model re-curtailment is 0.001/0.000/-0.003 % of potential against a reported 4.895 %, and 100.0/100.0/99.9 % of the +4.720/+5.057/+5.096 TWh wind residual IS the un-recurtailed gross-up. Solar is the control at -0.0003/-0.0003/-0.0032 TWh; the reconstruction closes to <=0.004 TWh. THE OWNER ANSWER, recorded here: MISO HSL data is NOT the fix. It would upgrade the bound's provenance to measured_potential and give a real hourly modelled-vs-reported benchmark, both worth having, but the LP already HOLDS the +4.9 % headroom and delivers 100 % of it, and a measured potential is HIGHER in exactly the congested hours, so the residual could grow. With slack and dump both 0.0000 TWh there is no channel to spill wind at all; the binding object is internal_congestion_split (G, miso-79 NO-BUILD fundamental, 88-99.7 % intra-LBA) at a model/measured zonal-spread compression of 0.083/0.126/0.164. Access is separately shut (misoenergy.org 5-minute workbooks allowlist-blocked, HTTP 403, docs/multi-iso/miso-data-audit.md). Probe scripts/probes/_miso234_wind_curtailment_phase0.py -> _miso234_wind_curtailment_phase0.json; record FINDING-miso234-the-south-seam-is-a-reporter-not-an-object-2026-09-07.md." },
