    measured_interface_limits: { cell: "R", ev: "miso-174 (2026-08-21, NO LP, no solve, keeper unchanged) — REFUTED at MISO on the pre-registered load-bearing kill K-PRE-1 of PREREG-miso174-seam-import-limit-precheck-2026-08-21.md (committed at 6cd0335 BEFORE the gated quantities were computed; miso-167 K-PRE-A pattern, miso-171 no-solve-adjudication precedent). Record FINDING-miso174-seam-overimport-adjudication-2026-08-21.md; instruments scripts/probes/_miso174_{seam_overimport_decomposition,import_limit_precheck,seam_price_evidence}.py + their _miso174_*.json records. THE KILL, at full strength: across ALL 72 scarce hours of 2023-2025 (summer, MISO's own RT > $200) the model's gross import NEVER ONCE exceeds the largest transfer that seam has been observed to deliver in the SAME (month x hour-of-day) bucket of the same year — PJM 0/11, 0/14, 0/47 and SPP 0/72, under BOTH the aligned and the production hour-key conventions, against a kill line of <20 % exceedance in >=2 of 3 years. Model gross import sits 26-29 % BELOW the observed ceiling on PJM (5.76 vs 7.75 / 4.16 vs 5.44 / 4.37 vs 6.16 GW). The test is conservative three ways against the kill (model GROSS vs measured NET; bucket max, not annual max; both hour keys). There is no capability violation to repair, so arming a limit here is a rule 1 [R-STRUCT] + rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH] breach. REPORTED AGAINST INTEREST: the lever is NOT rejected for being small — K-PRE-2 (reach) DOES NOT FIRE, an import ceiling could touch 2.74/2.25/2.97 GW against a 0.50 GW line. K-PRE-4 reaches the same verdict independently on data: no measured per-seam MW interface-limit series exists at our grain that is not already armed (the hourly derated limit is published by NOBODY — RDT Data Broker deprecated without archive, Data Exchange key-gated, adjudicated 2026-07-11/12; bc_HIST and pbc carry no MW limit and no flow; PJM's transfer_limits_and_flows is PJM-INTERNAL, none of its areas is the MISO seam; M2M flowgate ratings are branch x contingency grain with NO published PTDF, the standing M1 refutation, miso-77 §5.2; the EIA-930 directed-flow p90 envelope is ALREADY armed as miso_seam_flow_limit/miso_seam_export_limit). WHAT THE OBJECT ACTUALLY IS (evidence, not a new cell): the model's PJM-seam flow moves the WRONG WAY under stress — measured response in MISO's scarce hours vs its own summer mean is -0.77/-0.54/-1.03 GW while the model's is +0.89/+0.48/+1.34 GW, opposite sign in every year — with a huge unarbitraged spread present (MISO-facing PJM border hub $43/$57/$147 vs MISO RT $359/$374/$479) and the measured seam flow essentially UNCORRELATED with that spread all summer (r = +0.062/+0.047/-0.057). Not a ramp story either: the real seam is MORE volatile hour-to-hour than the model's (320-363 vs 142-172 MW mean |delta/h|). Manitoba is the control that makes the diagnosis specific — the one seam whose measured flow does respond to MISO scarcity (+0.57/+0.48/+1.19) is the one the model reproduces (+0.58/+0.82/+0.67), because it is carried by a firm contract block rather than spread arbitrage. This is a coincident-peak seam-RESPONSE object, covered by no existing cell: NOT import_shape_lever (MISO G), whose refusal is about hour-of-day price SHAPE and which miso-123 exonerated at r=+0.81..+0.996. DO-NOT-REDO: do not re-test a seam or zonal interface-LIMIT lever at MISO without new evidence defeating K-PRE-1 (i.e. a measured capability series showing the model exceeding deliverable transfer) or new data defeating K-PRE-4. The ZONAL-basis reading is separately refused on K-PRE-3(i) data admissibility (no LRZ-pair MW-limit series reconcilable without an invented apportionment) and sits inside the standing congestion adjudications internal_congestion_split G / zonal_loss_surface R — note it is NOT refused as redundant: the keeper's Midwest is a perfect copper plate (zonal price spread exactly 0.00 in all 8,760 h of all three years; separation exists only against MISO-South via the RDT, 2,432/2,705/5,086 h), so neither the 40,000 MW placeholder internal links nor the seasonal CIL/CEL groups ever bind." },
    internal_congestion_split: { cell: "G", ev: "miso-240 (2026-09-07, ZERO LP, no solve, keeper unchanged) CORROBORATES THE G ON A NEW INSTRUMENT AND DOES NOT RE-OPEN IT (rule 28(a) — not re-tested, and nothing here proposes a zonal split). POST-HOC and LABELLED in its own record, reading no gated quantity: on the keeper's OWN committed P1 duals the FOUR Midwest border zones (Illinois/Indiana/East/West) separate by more than $0.01 in 0.0002/0.0000/0.0000 of hours — i.e. the model's Midwest is ONE PRICE — while the MEASURED hub DA for the same four zones separates in 1.0000 of hours in every year, mean $8.75/$8.75/$11.25, p99 $35.25/$51.80/$54.14. The model's six-zone separation that does exist is the RDT/South and Plains boundary (0.2830/0.2732/0.4252 of hours, mean $0.91/$1.49/$2.86), not the Midwest. This is the same direction as miso-204's 'the model reproduces ~2 % of the actual dispersion' and miso-79's NO-BUILD, measured on price uniformity rather than on congestion mass. Record FINDING-miso240-the-external-bus-is-the-midwest-price-and-item-1-closes-2026-09-07.md §2a. PRIOR EV FOLLOWS: miso-78/79/80 miso-204 (2026-09-03, NO LP, no solve, keeper unchanged) MEASURES THE REPRESENTATION GAP IN THE OBJECT'S OWN HOURS AND STILL DOES NOT RE-OPEN THE G: in the 15 scarce hours of 2025 the eight trading hubs split by a mean max-min of $333.38 (vs $28.91 across all Jun-Jul, a ratio of 11.53) and EVERY DOLLAR of that split is MCC — MEC is hub-invariant to $0.02 in 100.00 % of all 8,760 hours of all three years — while the model's own six-zone spread in the same hours is $7.95, i.e. the model reproduces ~2 % of the actual dispersion. That is the KNOWN representation limit, now quantified where the lane cares, and miso-79's NO-BUILD stands FUNDAMENTAL (88-99.7 % of internal congestion mass is intra-LBA; an optimal simultaneous split of all six zones captures 1.9-3.8 %). Crucially the same session's G-1 verdict says the C3a residual is NOT congestion, so the dispersion gap is real and is NOT the C3a object — re-opening still needs RO-1 (published PTDFs / boundary-aligned limits) or RO-2. Record FINDING-miso204-the-tail-is-energy-and-the-comparator-is-one-hub-2026-09-03.md. THE NORTH-SOUTH CUT QUANTIFIED at miso-234 (2026-09-07, ZERO-LP, keeper unchanged, cell verdict UNCHANGED at G -- nothing tested, the G is corroborated). miso-204 measured the eight-trading-hub dispersion in 15 scarce hours; this is the ANNUAL, ALL-HOURS cut on the one boundary MISO's own market treats as a published constraint. Separation Indiana-South, mean|.|: measured 6.19/6.95/10.15 vs model 0.91/1.49/2.86 $/MWh (compression 0.148/0.215/0.281); p90|.| measured 13.56/14.20/24.29 vs model 3.53/4.02/9.18; corr(Indiana,South) measured +0.771/+0.854/+0.771 vs model +0.947/+0.891/+0.913. Whole-ISO six-zone max-min spread: model 0.91/1.49/2.86 vs measured 11.02/11.84/17.40 (compression 0.083/0.126/0.164), every zone inside $1 in 77.9/78.7/62.8 % of MODEL hours against 1.0/0.6/0.1 % measured. TWO KEEPER RESIDUALS ARE THE SAME OBJECT SEEN TWICE: the flat price field is why the LP re-curtails ZERO wind (see vre_reference_rate_curtailment_grossup) and why the South seam inherits the Midwest price's decile structure (see miso_south_export_ladder_rt_tail). RE-OPEN STILL NEEDS RO-1/RO-2 and this session supplies neither; miso-79's NO-BUILD stands fundamental (88-99.7 % of internal congestion mass is intra-LBA). Probes scripts/probes/_miso234_ns_separation_phase0.py and _miso234_wind_curtailment_phase0.py; record FINDING-miso234-the-south-seam-is-a-reporter-not-an-object-2026-09-07.md." },
