    miso_clean_tier_rows: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "ARM3-MEASURE 2026-08-09 (docs/handoffs/arm3-clean-row-horizon-2026-08-09.md), owner D-28 option A step 3 / sitting Addendum AF.3 — THE RAMP-YEAR MEASUREMENT (forecast pair miso-2031-2035-arm3-clean-{armed,ctrl}, keys 9337e00504e1e72a / cd2403cc031515db): both clean rows SLACK (dual 0) in EVERY year 2031-2035 INCLUDING 2035, the first MI-obligated year — but that inertness is a DEFECT, not a market fact. model/lp/rows.py::_build_rps_region_rows zone-masks a region WIND/SOLAR columns and appends its region_gen_idx columns with NO zone filter, and _resolve_clean_region_gen_idx(fleet, region_fuels) is never given the mask (it filters by FUEL alone over the whole fleet), so each clean row nuclear/hydro/biomass/CCS credit is ISO-WIDE while its VRE credit is in-mask: the Michigan East-only row is satisfied by MISO-SOUTH nuclear — the very Iowa-surplus-pays-the-Michigan-bill defect Arm 2 exists to remove, and it defeats the cited basis of the row (MCL 460.1029, in-state restriction). MI 2035 as built 139.112 TWh vs RHS 95.771 -> SLACK; zone-masked 53.324 TWh -> WOULD BIND at the 30 USD/MWh ACP; leak 85.788 TWh (MN leaks 49.056 TWh/yr but its 5-zone mask keeps it slack either way). ARM-3 EXCLUSIVE — the Arm-2 RPS call passes no region_gen_idx, so miso_rps_compliance_regions is UNAFFECTED and its duals are identical across the pair ([0,30,0,30,0] in all five years). Arming changes NOTHING: retirements, thermal and renewable additions and fleet_by_fuel_after are identical to the digit every year, which is also the E-1 no-build-limb behavioural check. The 45U composition seam is INERT here under every mask reading — 45U terminates after 2032 (26 U.S.C. 45U(e)) and MI cannot bind before 2035, so the composition delta measured at HEAD is exactly 0.0000 USD/MWh at every (P,D) from 2033 on; the arming question is COMPOSITION-INDEPENDENT. MN mask sensitivity (owner-open, FFR-7B-2 3.2): under the shipped 5-zone Midwest footprint MN is covered in every ramp year; under the in-state West-only reading it is short 27.1-42.4 TWh in ALL five and would pin at 30 USD. VERDICT STAYS O (NOT I): the measured inertness is wiring-driven, so the mechanism has not yet been validly tested and ARMING IS BLOCKED pending the mask fix — that fix is a separate charter and was deliberately NOT made in the measuring session. NOTE: this row previously filed MISO evidence under the CAISO key (ev.C); re-keyed to M per the header schema. FFR-7B-2 (docs/handoffs/ffr-7b2-rps-krow-clean-rows-2026-08-06.md); design FFR-6B §6 (docs/handoffs/ffr-6b-rps-grain-clean-tiers-2026-08-05.md); charter FFR-7B §6.2 (docs/handoffs/ffr-7b-rps-clean-tier-repair-2026-08-06.md); owner D-22(a) sitting Addendum V.6/X.3 2026-08-06. ARM3-FIX 2026-08-10 (docs/handoffs/arm3-fix-zone-mask-2026-08-09.md): THE MASK DEFECT IS FIXED — _resolve_clean_region_gen_idx now takes the region's eligible_zone_mask and admits a generator only when its fuel qualifies AND its zone is in-mask, the same filter the builder applies to W/S columns (filter at index construction, rule 2; builder untouched; the Arm-2 RPS call still passes no region_gen_idx and the family is proven append-only by test; the default path is proven unable to reach the resolver, pinned default cache key 603c2498bf71d21d unmoved; no ScenarioConfig field added). RE-MEASURED on the identical committed prereg pair (miso-2031-2035-arm3fix-clean-{armed,ctrl}, keys UNCHANGED 9337e00504e1e72a / cd2403cc031515db, all ten year-solves Optimal): MI's row BINDS at 2035 — its first statutory obligation year — pinned at the 30 USD ACP ceiling (in-mask 57.351 TWh vs RHS 95.771; the control's 53.327 reproduces the finding's offline-corrected 53.324 to 0.006 %; the binding row PULLS +4.02 TWh of clean energy in-mask, a real price response); MN slack all five years under the shipped 5-zone mask (in-state counterfactual still SHORT 27.1-41.9 TWh every year — the owner's open mask reading stays decisive for MN); Arm-2 RPS duals bit-stable [0,30,0,30,0] in every year of BOTH legs; capacity events identical to the digit every year (E-1 price-only holds — the 2035 dual first reaches a screen in 2036, outside the window; 2031-2034 objective deltas reproduce the defective pair's alternate-optima noise byte-identically, so on slack rows the fix is a proven no-op in the solve); 2035 objective +1.1746 bn USD (+4.84 %) = 38.420 TWh ACP shortfall x 30 USD + ~22 M USD true redispatch, lw price -0.39 USD/MWh, co2 +0.77 Mt. Composition-independence CONFIRMED on a binding row (dual at the ceiling where all defensible 45U compositions coincide to the cent; 45U dead from 2033 regardless). VERDICT STAYS O: the mechanism is now validly wired, validly tested, and the evidence is card-grade — but arming is the owner's D-28 step-3 decision, not this session's ARM-3-ARM 2026-08-11 (docs/handoffs/PREREG-arm3-arm-miso-clean-tier-2026-08-11.md, docs/handoffs/arm3-arm-miso-clean-tier-2026-08-11.md): OWNER CARD D-29 SIGNED (sitting Addendum AK.8) and EXECUTED — miso_clean_tier_rows is now the MISO FORECAST DEFAULT, armed through MISO's ISOConfig.default_scenario_overrides, the SAME seam D-26 used for Arm 2, NOT a ScenarioConfig field-default flip (which would arm all six ISOs, a rule-25 violation, and break the strict Arm-2 dependency for the five that never carry the K-row grain). Forecast-scoped at CONSUMPTION (runner.py requires mode == forecast; run_calibration_full.py never applies ISO overrides), so the backcast lane and the MISO keeper are untouched. THIS IS A DECLARED CACHE EPOCH FOR THE MISO FORECAST LANE: the resolved default key moves cd2403cc031515db -> 9337e00504e1e72a, so every pre-arm MISO forecast bundle is superseded and NONE is silently re-used (the armed value differs from the registered _CACHE_KEY_OPTIONAL_FIELDS field default and therefore enters the digest); the GLOBAL pinned default key 603c2498bf71d21d is UNMOVED, verified by scripts/probes/_arm3arm_cache_epoch.py and by the CI pin. Both poles reproduce the SIGNED ARM3-FIX pair's keys byte-exactly at HEAD, so the armed default resolves to the very scenario the signed evidence measured. CONSEQUENCE recorded before the fact: once armed, NO CLI invocation can reach a clean-tier-OFF MISO forecast leg (apply_iso_scenario_defaults re-arms any field left at its ScenarioConfig default and --miso-clean-tier-rows is store_true with no negative form), so the arm-off pole is permanently the COMMITTED ARM3-FIX control bundle, never a re-solve — the same caveat entry_vre_capacity_revenue and Arm 2 already carry. VERDICT O -> K." },
